;; proper-tail-calls T4 (docs/upcoming/proper-tail-calls-plan.md, T-D3): the
;; codegen snapshot for a backedge taken through an owned local's drop glue.
;;
;; This program was `errors/tailcall-owned-local-live` until T4 -- a negative
;; whose header predicted its own move: "`b` is never passed to the recursive
;; call and is dead at that point, so T4 would legally move the drop before the
;; call and restore tail position."  It did.  That fixture now holds a local
;; that is genuinely live across the call.
;;
;; What the snapshot pins, in the emitted `with_hyref`:
;;
;;   - `__tur_tailcall:` at the top and `goto __tur_tailcall;` in the else arm;
;;   - the frame is still declared and the drop still pushed on it -- so a
;;     panic in an argument fires it through the panic return;
;;   - `tur_frame_fire_lifo` runs AFTER the argument temps and BEFORE the
;;     parameter reassignment, and before the `return` in the base case.

(defn with-ref [n : int] : int
  (let [b (ref 1)]
    (if (= n 0)
      0
      ^tailcall (with-ref (- n 1)))))

(defn main [] : int
  (println (with-ref 3))
  0)
